From 00f24832223a0f847aad1513d78dc8a6db7cae2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:04:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 124/125] dynarmic: shared page walks for fastmem's declined
 accesses only (A64); plain load-acquires; no barrier for DMB LD/ST;
 descriptor from a kept FPCR part

A64 with fastmem grouped every run of accesses through one base into one page table walk (about
18 instructions, then a test and a branch per access), where folded fastmem is a cmp, a jae and
the access: now only the accesses fastmem was declined for share walks
(A64SharedWalkForSlowAccesses after Optimize, from the emitter's list), as A32's. With
plain_acquire_loads a load-acquire is a mov (the C++ seq_cst mapping: the store-release is an
xchg) instead of lock xadd; elide_load_store_only_barriers drops DMB of the LD or ST type. The
location descriptor for indirect jumps and return stack misses is the PC masked, or'd with
fpcr_descriptor_bits (kept by SetFpcr). game.c for AArch64: -8.4% instructions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
